<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Shipyard: third-party licences</title>
<style>
body { font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 60rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; color: #1b1f24; background: #fff; }
pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f4f5f7; padding: 1rem; font-size: 13px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e8eb; background: #15181c; } pre { background: #1f2329; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party licences</h1>
<p>Shipyard is Apache-2.0. It is built with the software below, under these licences: each licence's text once, with what uses it. Each crate's source, as built, is at https://crates.io/crates/NAME/VERSION (as a licence such as MPL-2.0 asks).</p>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}<li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}</ul>
{{#each licenses}}
<h2 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h2>
<p>Used by:</p>
<ul>
{{#each used_by}}<li>{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}{{#if crate.repository}} (<a href="{{crate.repository}}">{{crate.repository}}</a>){{/if}}</li>
{{/each}}</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
